{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Pull Request.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Pull Request.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"pull request pull request","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Pull Request.md","fileName":"Pull Request.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Pull Request","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 11:48\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Continuous Delivery Risk and Release Governance]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Continuous Delivery Risk and Release Governance","hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Pull Request.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Pull Request.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"pull request pull request","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Pull Request.md","fileName":"Pull Request.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Pull Request","heading":"Pull Request","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A pull request proposes merging one branch's changes into another and provides a boundary for discussion, automated checks, and approval before integration. It makes the exact diff and its delivery evidence visible to reviewers.\n\nThe request improves control only when review and validation are meaningful. Automatically approving a change or allowing required checks to be bypassed preserves the interface without the safeguard.\n\nAI can summarize metadata, explain failures, and flag possible risk inside this boundary, but it remains advisory. Deterministic checks and accountable reviewers decide whether the proposed change is acceptable.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Continuous Delivery Risk and Release Governance","hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Pull Request.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - F